a, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify that a fault while reading/resolving the specific signing key's public counterpart during mint is handled without aborting the sign (e.g. logged/degraded to a warning), preserving the existing sign flow, and add a test for it.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.785,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Testing covers 'a resolution fault is surfaced as degraded (not swallowed)' only for the startup/health check, not the mint path","AC1: 'it still returns the signature (no refusal, no existing sign flow broken)' — but a raised exception in the guard would break the flow"],"finding":"The mint-time guard (AC1) does not specify behavior when its own public-key read/resolution faults (e.g. _read_opcert_pub raises); since the guard must never break the existing sign flow, a fault in the guard itself must be caught and not abort signing, but this is unspecified.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0883facd44b8e871","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach item 1 / AC1 / Testing","norm_id":"ne19e41241ac71902","priority":0.165,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["_read_opcert_pub(key_path) raises during a mint because the resolved key path is unreadable/absent"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add to Approach item 1 and Testing: if _read_opcert_pub(key_path) faults, catch it and emit the same WARNING (or a resolution-fault variant) while still returning the signature; add a unit test that a pub-read fault at mint warns but does not raise.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_wor