y_cannot_resolve(tracker, key_path, principal)' is CALLED inside mint_opcert_record after ensure_opcert_key resolves key_path","The helper cites the SAME bug id this plan is filed under: 'See bug 879b-9bf0-86fd-4a6b'"],"finding":"The plan's central premise — that Gerrit 2337 'did NOT add any GUARD' and that 'sign_manifest still mints a certificate without checking that the environment can resolve a public counterpart' — is refuted by the codebase: the mint-time guard already exists AND is wired into the mint path.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f59afa414892940ed","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Context/Problem section; AC1; AC2; DD1","norm_id":"nadeeff5566469229","priority":0.8,"reason":"veto:plan-goal-satisfied","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer takes this plan and re-implements a guard that already exists and is live","AC1/AC2 written RED-then-GREEN tests are already GREEN before any change, so DD1's 'RED before the change' cannot be satisfied"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Verify the current main HEAD: if the guard is present and wired, close AC1/AC2/DD1 as already-implemented (or redefine the plan around a genuinely absent gap, e.g. covering the HMAC/`sign_opcert_manifest` path if that lacks the guard).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile the Problem statement and AC3/DD2 with the fact that `opcert_signing_status`/`opcert_signer_degraded`/`run_startup_opcert_check` (src/rebar/_mcp_health.py:298-386, cited to bug 879b) already implement the pinned-key DEGRADED field + boot WARNING and are already wired (line 548) and surfaced on `/health` (line 407) — either descope AC3 as already-landed or specify the concrete residual gap.","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":0.0,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan asserts: 'nothing at deploy/startup surfaces it when it cannot' and proposes 'the MCP server's existing health surface reports a DEGRADED field and logs a boot WARNING when the bound startup signer's public key is not the pinned trusted-environment key'","src/rebar/_mcp_health.py:298-349 opcert_signing_status implements the pinned-trusted-env-key match (expected gated on load_trusted_environments; comment-insensitive _ssh_pub_body match against trusted_env_keyring; RemovedInputError re-raise; error field on fault), citing 'bug 879b'","src/rebar/_mcp_health.py:352-362 opcert_signer_degraded and 365-386 run_startup_opcert_check log the serve-degraded boot WARNING naming the principal, 'boot continues', citing 'bug 879b-9bf0-86fd-4a6b'","src/rebar/_mcp_health.py:548 run_startup_opcert_check(opcert_binding) is wired into boot; line 407 the /health route surfaces the 'opcert' field"],"finding":"The plan asserts 'nothing at deploy/startup surfaces it' and proposes AC3's startup/health serve-degraded surface as new work, but the MCP health surface already implements and wires exactly that pinned-key degraded check.","group_criteria":null,"group