00 even when auth is enabled'","register_health_route (_mcp_health.py:295-308) returns JSONResponse({'in_flight':..., 'store': store_status()}) with no auth","Plan AC3: 'reports a DEGRADED opcert field and logs a boot WARNING' — placement (public /health body vs. boot log only) and field contents are left unspecified, whereas AC1's WARNING contents are explicitly named","ANTI-FP note: key paths and the public principal/trusted_env keys are non-secret, so this is an undeclared-posture ambiguity, not a secret-leak (no HIGH class fires)"],"finding":"AC3 adds a DEGRADED `opcert` field to the MCP health surface (`_mcp_health.py`), whose existing `/health` route is deliberately unauthenticated and network-reachable (registered outside RequireAuthMiddleware), but the plan does not declare whether that degraded field is exposed on the unauthenticated `/health` JSON body reachable by a lower-trust probe or confined to boot logs, nor what the field contains.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fce35e0a4ac69367c","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 2 / AC3 (`the MCP server's existing health surface (src/rebar/_mcp_health.py)`)","norm_id":"ncda0fe6d48583d32","priority":0.2406,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":true,"scenarios":[],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"In AC3, state explicitly that the degraded signal is either (a) confined to the boot WARNING log plus an authenticated/internal readiness path, OR (b) a boolean/enum status field on public /health carrying no key material (no key path), matching the existing non-sensitive in_flight/store fields — and record the deliberate public-with-rationale choice.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.4375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessaril